mlir provides CMake targets:

    find_package(MLIR REQUIRED CONFIG)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE MLIRIR MLIRSupport)

MLIR is a static build: there is no libMLIR.so or libLLVM.so, so the component
archives in lib/ are linked directly.

The LLVM and MLIR exported targets deliberately carry no
INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES, so include paths come from the config variables:

    include_directories(${MLIR_INCLUDE_DIRS} ${LLVM_INCLUDE_DIRS})
    add_definitions(${LLVM_DEFINITIONS})
    if(NOT LLVM_ENABLE_RTTI)
      add_compile_options(-fno-rtti)
    endif()

MLIRConfig.cmake sits in lib/cmake/mlir rather than share/mlir/cmake, because
both it and LLVMConfig.cmake derive their install prefix by walking up from their
own file. The vcpkg toolchain finds it with no extra settings. Set
MLIR_DIR=<prefix>/lib/cmake/mlir only for a consumer that does not use that
toolchain.

Tablegen is available: MLIRConfig already points MLIR_TABLEGEN_EXE and
MLIR_PDLL_TABLEGEN_EXE at this package's bin/, so a dialect project needs no
PATH setup. Note that FileCheck, not, count and split-file are absent, so a
lit-based test suite cannot run against this package alone.
